{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mgzcr7rrtems2q56ffwtlns7redxqxtsai2bq4izkfujtfasimya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Result\n\n**60 differential tests + 5 exhaustive stress sweeps, all passing** in every configuration. Both libraries are loaded via `libloading` and driven only through `dlsym`; stdout is captured at the **fd level** so the comparison is byte-for-byte through the real FFI boundary.\n\n### Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | ✅ `T` sets are *identical*, not merely a superset |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row (30) passes randomized | ✅ 32 tests |\n| Binary stdout comparison | ✅ N/A — no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]`; asserted by `d06` |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row (18 + 4 generic) | ✅ 22 tests |\n| All of the above under every feature combo | ✅ `run_all_features.sh`: 4/4 PASS |\n\n### Two real issues found and fixed\n\n1. **Harness bug (not the translation):** libtest's own progress lines leaked into fd-level captures from parallel threads → 11 false divergences. Fixed by pinning `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` in `.cargo/config.toml` and draining *both* buffers (Rust's `LineWriter` **and** glibc's `FILE *stdout`) before redirecting.\n\n2. **`bad()`'s OOB write relied on Rust UB.** The translation derived its base pointer from the `buffer` field, so `offset(data)` for `data >= 10` was out of that pointer's provenance — undefined in Rust and liable to be optimized away at higher opt levels. Rewrote it to take provenance from the whole `Frame` and bound the store to the frame's slack. Behavior for every *defined* C input is unchanged; the emulation is now robust rather than luck.\n\n### Key C behavior I replicated rather than \"fixed\"\n\nI disassembled the C `.so` to establish the real frame layout (`buffer` base `-0x30(%rbp)`, `sub $0x40,%rsp`) instead of guessing. This matters because `bad()` has **no upper-bound check**:\n\n- `data` 10 → hits frame padding `-0x8(%rbp)`\n- `data` 11 → hits the loop counter `i` at `-0x4(%rbp)`, which `i = 0` then overwrites\n\nBoth print **ten zeros and no error message** — genuinely defined, so they're asserted. `data >= 12` overwrites the saved `%rbp`/return address; that's true UB, so it is documented in `ERRORS.md` row 9 and excluded from assertion, with `BAD_MAX_DEFINED = 11` bounding every randomized sweep. I did not add the missing bounds check.\n\nAlso worth noting: both compilers independently rewrite `printf(\"%s\\n\", x)` into `puts(x)`, so `printLine(\"%n%n%n\")` prints verbatim in both — `cfg04`/`err03` pin this, since a divergence here would be an arbitrary-write primitive.\n\n### Files\n\n- `translation/{SYMBOLS,ERRORS,CONFIGS}.md` — Phase A artifacts\n- `translation/tests/harness/mod.rs` — dual-`.so` loader, fd capture, seeded PRNG\n- `translation/tests/{phase_b_valid,phase_c_errors,phase_d_symbols,stress_exhaustive}.rs`\n- `translation/run_all_features.sh` — derives the feature power set from `Cargo.toml` (no hard-coding) and cross-runs it against both profiles\n\nOne caveat: the sandbox has no network, so I added `offline = true` to `translation/.cargo/config.toml` to resolve `libloading` from the local cargo cache. `c_src/` is unmodified (only the gitignored `build/` directory was added by the required cmake build)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":99650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":548,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45d23f69-7b50-4010-9d52-e62f67e67dd5","uuid":"dc49dcd9-e5c9-41b3-9b35-10dd42513f0e","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:15:39.152Z"}
